Step 8 — Joker windows, early end, Bound declaration, callouts, scoring

Behavior to implement

Joker free-play windows:

True on: Bid = 9 (tricks 7–9), or Bid = 7 and Bound declared (tricks 7–9).

In these windows: jokers may be played on any card, ignoring follow-suit; BJ may lead; RJ may lead only after BJ has appeared.

Early end of hand:

Success early if bidder’s team tricks >= BID.

Fail early if defenders’ tricks > 9 - BID.

Bound (only for Bid=7):

After trick 6, if bidder’s team is 6–0, bidder may declare Bound; flips the joker window on for 7–9.

Callouts (illegal cut / not following suit):

Can be made only after trick 1 has finished; can only target a completed trick.

No violations during joker windows.

Scoring for a correct/false call:

Low contracts (5–8): ±15, hand does not end.

High contracts (Bound(7) or 9): ±36, hand ends immediately.

Scoring summary:

Normal success: +BID to bidding team.

Normal fail (6–8): +2×BID to defenders.

Malzoom fail (bid 5 by shuffler): +5 to defenders; success: +5 to bidding team.

Bid 9 success/fail: +36 to winner/defenders.

Bound success/fail: +36 / +18.

Tests you should write

Window logic flips correctly for (9) and (7 with Bound).

